ahaziah_121	Ahaziah	\N	Ahaziah, son of Jehoram	Jehoahaz; Azariah	Male	Jerusalem	Jerusalem	-907	-885	907 BC	885 BC	\N	Old Testament	f	Tribe of Judah	Genealogy of Jesus	The son of Joram, or Jehoram, and sixth king of Judah. Called Jehoahaz (2 Chr. 21:17; 25:23), and Azariah (2 Chr. 22:6). Guided by his idolatrous mother Athaliah, his reign was disastrous (2 Kings 8:24-29; 9:29). He joined his uncle Jehoram, king of Israel, in an expedition against Hazael, king of Damascus; but was wounded at the pass of Gur when attempting to escape, and had strength only to reach Megiddo, where he died (2 Kings 9:22-28). He reigned only one year.	Easton's Bible Dictionary	2 Kings 8:24	26	rec83PZfB7PGjHMh0	King	King
