merab_2001	Merab	\N	Merab	Michal	Female	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Old Testament	f	\N	\N	Increase, the eldest of Saul’s two daughters (1 Sam. 14:49). She was betrothed to David after his victory over Goliath, but does not seem to have entered heartily into this arrangement (18:2, 17, 19). She was at length, however, married to Adriel of Abel-Meholah, a town in the Jordan valley, about 10 miles south of Bethshean, with whom the house of Saul maintained alliance. She had five sons, who were all put to death by the Gibeonites on the hill of Gibeah (2 Sam. 21:8).	Easton's Bible Dictionary	1 Samuel 14:49	4	recHM6hYE0iNCs2jz	\N	Person
