COPY bible.relationship_type (relationship_type, category, is_symmetric, description) FROM stdin;
Begot	Family	f	Subject is a parent (father or mother) of the object.
Married	Family	t	Subject and object were husband and wife (includes concubines where the source records a union).
SiblingOf	Family	t	Subject and object share both parents (full siblings).
HalfSiblingOf	Family	t	Subject and object share one parent.
Adopted	Family	f	Subject raised the object as their own child.
Succeeded	Office	f	Subject succeeded the object in an office (throne, priesthood, prophetic or apostolic office).
Anointed	Office	f	Subject anointed the object for an office (king, priest).
Appointed	Office	f	Subject appointed the object to a position or task.
Commissioned	Office	f	Subject charged, sent or called the object to a mission.
Served	Allegiance	f	Subject served the object as servant, official, soldier or assistant.
Followed	Allegiance	f	Subject followed the object as disciple, adherent or loyal supporter.
Accompanied	Allegiance	f	Subject travelled with or ministered alongside the object.
Mentored	Allegiance	f	Subject taught, trained or guided the object.
Opposed	Conflict	f	Subject opposed, conspired against or rebelled against the object.
Pursued	Conflict	f	Subject hunted or chased the object.
Defeated	Conflict	f	Subject defeated the object (or the object's forces) in battle.
Captured	Conflict	f	Subject took the object captive.
Imprisoned	Conflict	f	Subject put the object in prison or custody.
Exiled	Conflict	f	Subject banished or expelled the object.
Sentenced	Conflict	f	Subject condemned or ordered the execution or punishment of the object.
Killed	Conflict	f	Subject killed the object, directly or by order.
Betrayed	Conflict	f	Subject betrayed the trust of the object.
Deceived	Conflict	f	Subject deliberately misled the object.
Denied	Conflict	f	Subject publicly disowned the object.
Freed	Deliverance	f	Subject released the object from captivity, prison or slavery.
Rescued	Deliverance	f	Subject saved or protected the object from danger.
Healed	Deliverance	f	Subject healed the object of illness or affliction.
RaisedFromDead	Deliverance	f	Subject raised the object from death.
Baptized	Religious	f	Subject baptized the object.
Blessed	Religious	f	Subject pronounced a blessing on the object.
Cursed	Religious	f	Subject pronounced a curse or judgment on the object.
Rebuked	Religious	f	Subject rebuked or confronted the object for wrongdoing.
WroteTo	Religious	f	Subject addressed a letter or book to the object.
\.
